  - clinical decision support
abstract: >-
  A resource of 797 candidate non-interacting drug pairs over 161 drugs, in
  which each pair carries a quantified FAERS co-exposure denominator, the
  minimum reporting odds ratio that co-exposure count could have detected, and
  an evidence tier derived from both by a published, machine-checked rule. The
  release ships the drug-degree metadata and matched-sampling protocol needed
  to measure how much of a predictor's apparent performance is attributable to
  drug popularity rather than to pharmacology: a popularity-only heuristic
  reaches AUC 0.934 against random negatives and 0.947 against these curated
  negatives, but 0.498 - chance - once negatives are degree-matched. The
  resource is for evaluation and benchmarking only; it licenses no clinical
  decision. It supersedes a retracted predecessor
  (doi:10.1155/2022/8904342, retracted doi:10.1155/2023/9892301), which is
  used here solely as an object of audit.
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Anti-DDI Resource: A Dataset for Potential Negative Reported Interaction
      Combinations to Improve Medical Research and Decision-Making
    authors:
